__pycache__/
*.pyc
# The article database stays off the repo while it is public. It holds the
# papers' own headlines and standfirsts - 57,000 words of somebody else's
# copy - and pushing that is republishing, which is the one thing the plan
# commits us never to do. The frames are fine: story names we wrote
# ourselves, plus numbers.
#
# The cost is that the archive then lives on one machine, and the
# observation table is the part that cannot be rebuilt. Back it up. When
# the repo goes private, drop these two lines and commit it.
data/ingest.sqlite
data/*.sqlite-wal
data/*.sqlite-shm
data/view.html
data/cacert.pem
.venv/
.env
.env.*
